-- title:
--   Actual controlled ruin-stopped centered intrinsic jump term with the unique physical predictable clock and no initial compensator premise
-- statement:
--   On the original SpectrallyNegativeLevy jump-counting kernel of the same risk process, eliminate the initial-time stopped compensator rectangle assumption from the canonical Chat02-C controlled negative-jump mean-zero theorem. Demand instead that its exact rightCont predictable clock agrees with finite-horizon physical Lebesgue time times P. The canonical Chat01 initial source jump law and measure-ext uniqueness supply the missing initial rectangle for the same μ, while the genuine right-continuous future source law and band local finiteness remain visible premises. The conclusion is the full stopped source Taylor kernel measurability, L1 integrability of raw and compensated jump integrals and exact zero expectation.
